 and the allow-list behavior still works correctly (opsadmin allowed, a fresh test user denied).","actions_performed":["Inspected OS, existing users, and cron.allow/cron.deny state on node1","Created local user opsadmin (useradd -m)","Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing exactly 'root' and 'opsadmin', mode 644 root:root","Verified functionally: opsadmin and root can create crontabs; a disposable testuser is denied with cronie's standard rejection message","Cleaned up test crontabs and removed the disposable testuser","Captured healthy baseline: boot_id, crond active/enabled, cron.allow contents","Restarted node1 via 'systemctl reboot' (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned; confirmed boot_id changed, proving an actual restart","Post-restart verified crond active/enabled, /etc/cron.allow persisted (root, opsadmin), and functional allow/deny behavior still correct against a fresh verifyuser","Cleaned up verifyuser and confirmed no leftover crontabs"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs (cron.allow configured)","command_ids":["cmd-53b7bfe3932d4379","cmd-aeb030c966c445cb","cmd-a295a07119514b2c"],"summary":"Confirmed no pre-existing cron.allow/opsadmin user, created opsadmin, wrote /etc/cron.allow with root and opsadmin"},{"requirement":"Functional proof: allowed users succeed, others are denied","command_ids":["cmd-20b5c673ae3344b9"],"summary":"sudo -u opsadmin crontab succeeded (rc=0) and installed a job; sudo -u testuser crontab was rejected with 'not allowed to use this program' (rc=1); root also succeeded"},{"requirement":"Test artifacts cleaned up","command_ids":["cmd-216be52e0ba94441","cmd-c2d945c342424fd6"],"summary":"Removed test crontabs for opsadmin/root and deleted testuser after killing its lingering session"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-2e93e639a75e40cf"],"summary":"Captured boot_id cce73776-a7f7-4f32-b822-95d105c52a64, crond active/enabled, and cron.allow contents (root, opsadmin) prior to restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-a1ce5ab3e4664ee5"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'systemctl reboot' via nohup+disown; command returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately"},{"requirement":"Proof of changed boot identity (actual restart, not just downtime)","command_ids":["cmd-36e66f0a7d644497","cmd-88015f01bed042c0","cmd-1bad2a463b75460a","cmd-a2cc62af4fb9474c","cmd-7acd2a36f7a44af8"],"summary":"Node became unreachable (connection timed out/reset) during reboot, then reconnected with a new boot_id 273bc930-4571-4fe4-9f28-c93141f9f8da, differing from the pre-restart value"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of cron access control and service health","command_ids":["cmd-25bd9604e9c04aa3","cmd-226ae8d954534367"],"summary":"crond active/enabled after reboot, /etc/cron.allow persisted with root and opsadmin, opsadmin successfully scheduled a cron job while a fresh verifyuser was denied; cleanup confirmed"}]},"ttft_ms":1589,"type":"result","duration_ms":64507,"uuid":"95addfc9-7e82-4334-b145-42ca47e68ac1","ttft_stream_ms":731,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":731,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
